  "body": "**What happens:** `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` `onProbeResult` writes each deviation as\n`\"#\" + n + \"=\" + mean + \"-\" + fu(expected)`. When the expected value (in the active work offset) is negative, the post writes a doubled sign, e.g. `#190=#100--0.0787`. Edge and outside-corner probes hit this; the bore/boss centre in the committed golden does not, so no golden shows it.\n\nWhether a Fanuc macro-B control accepts `--` is not documented in any public reference we have. The same pattern was refused-adjacent on LinuxCNC: PathPilot Hub rejected the unbracketed form outright (PR #376).\n\n**Expected:** fold the sign into the operator (`#190=#100+0.0787`), and optionally bracket the expression (`#190=[#100+0.0787]`, valid macro B). Pin it with an edge-mode golden.\n\nFound while Hub-testing #362 (PR #376, fixed there in 6e246c8). The #173 posts (Haas, Mazak, Sinumerik; PR #360) copy the pattern and are fixed on that branch.\n",
